Step 1 — Download and Install UTM

Because I am using an Apple Silicon Mac (M1), I used UTM instead of VirtualBox for better ARM compatibility.

Process
Downloaded UTM from the official website
Installed the application on macOS
Opened UTM and created a new virtual machine


Step 2 — Download Ubuntu ARM ISO

I downloaded the ARM64 version of Ubuntu because Apple Silicon Macs use ARM architecture.

Important Lesson

Intel/AMD Ubuntu ISOs can cause boot and compatibility issues on M1 Macs.

Step 3 — Create Ubuntu Virtual Machine

Inside UTM:

Created a new Linux virtual machine
Selected the Ubuntu ARM ISO
Configured system resources
VM Configuration
Setting	Value
RAM	4 GB
CPU Cores	2
Storage	40 GB
Storage Type	Dynamically Allocated


Step 4 — Install Ubuntu

During installation:

skipped internet setup initially
enabled third-party software/drivers
